    Hedging patterns are inverted from typical: ember hedges upward ("i'm not sure if i'm going to be able to get to use you at all," "i don't want to unpack the whole thing") rather than hedging claims downward. The hedging is about self-permission, not about epistemic uncertainty. They know what they think; they're uncertain about whether they're allowed to think it.
