host!: publish adopted bases through fresh segment identities (HOST-71)

Separate physical identity from logical offset. The authenticated atomic base
selects a segment generation; adoption creates its header under a fresh identity
and retains its logical offset as the new run start. An interruption before
publication leaves the previous base and every file it selects unchanged.
Normal seals and rotations preserve the selected generation and headerFault.

