## HOST-69 · the writer-life induction as ONE theorem: `WriterLife` over the abstract events (open, admitted fold, seal) and `writer_life_trusted` (2026-10-20, HOST-22; HOST-64's "NOT PROVED: the writer-life induction as one theorem", cv 01a1583d-864c item 5)

**Decision.** `Host.Proofs.Trusted` gains `WriterLife keys file₀ fileN`, an inductive Prop: `refl`, or a `link` = one `openWith` of the base file to `o`, an admitted fold `World.fold X.env o.opened.world l = .ok w'`, and `Base.file … w' … = .ok file'` (with `ix.count < 2^64`), then the life from `file'`. `writer_life_trusted`: over a life from a base file whose World is trusted at `r`, the base file it ends at holds a World trusted at `r` (`link_trusted` = `openWith_trusted` → `trusted_fold` → `sealed_trusted`, by induction). Starts: `genesis_life_trusted` (at `w₀.origin`, through `genesis_trusted` and `genesisImage_trusted`) and `import_life_trusted` (at the pinned `o`, `import_trusted_pinned`). Consumer: `life_opened_size_le` (every reopen of a base the life ends at holds a World within `worldBytesMax`). Tooth: `life_refutes_potential` (a reached base holding more than `potentialMax` refutes the life from a trusted start; each premise load-bearing: `refl` at `file₀ = fileN` without `hp`, a low-potential start without `hbase`).

